# Tiny edge in front of slurmrestd.
#
# Why a sidecar at all: conoha-proxy probes its upstream at GET /openapi/v3
# (per conoha.yml) and only accepts 2xx as healthy. slurmrestd itself
# requires JWT auth on every endpoint including /openapi/v3, so the
# probe never reaches 2xx without per-request tokens. Caddy here answers
# /healthz with a plain 200 so the proxy can decide health, while
# reverse-proxying everything else to slurmrestd:6820 untouched (the
# JWT-aware client passes X-SLURM-USER-* headers through).
:6820 {
	# Probe endpoint for conoha-proxy.
	@probe path /healthz
	handle @probe {
		respond "ok" 200
	}
	# Everything else (the real API surface) goes through to slurmrestd
	# with all headers preserved.
	reverse_proxy slurmrestd:6820
}
